+# UI Specification: Review selection state
+
+**Story**: S007  
+**Epic**: E001-capture-review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-10  
+**Version**: 1.0
+
+## Design Context Sources
+
+No project design system, UX strategy, wireframes, project profile, or active recipe is present in this workspace. The implementation therefore uses native controls and browser defaults rather than inventing a visual language.
+
+## PROFILE surface impact
+
+- [x] No — no declared PROFILE surface is available in this workspace.
+
+## Visual Assets Requirements
+
+- [x] No — this story needs no visual assets.
+
+## Component Overview
+
+**Component Name**: Review list  
+**Type**: Modified composite  
+**Design System Reference**: Native HTML controls  
+**Affects**: `web/index.html` review surface
+
+## Visual Specifications
+
+### Component Anatomy
+
+```
+main#review (aria-live="polite")
+└── button.review-item (one per item, aria-pressed)
+button#approve (disabled until selection exists)
+```
+
+### Dimensions and properties
+
+- The list is fluid within the page; each control has at least a 44px target height.
+- Native button styling is retained so focus, pressed, disabled, and high-contrast browser behavior remain legible without unsupported design tokens.
+- Selected items use `aria-pressed="true"`; confirmed items remain listed but are disabled.
+
+## States & Behavior
+
+| State | Review list | Approve action |
+|---|---|---|
+| Empty | Announces that there are no items to review | Disabled |
+| Pending, unselected | Enabled button with `aria-pressed="false"` | Disabled |
+| Pending, selected | Enabled button with `aria-pressed="true"` | Enabled |
+| Confirmed | Disabled button, labelled as confirmed | Disabled unless another pending item is selected |
+| Loading/error | Not applicable: all transitions are synchronous in-memory operations | Not applicable |
+
+- Click, Enter, and Space use the native button activation behavior to toggle a pending item.
+- Activating Approve confirms only selected items and clears selection.
+- The action has no asynchronous submit path, so a pending spinner, double-submit lock, and status message are not applicable.
+
+## Responsive Behavior
+
+- Mobile, tablet, desktop, and wide layouts retain one vertically stacked review list and one primary action.
+- The first viewport has one primary action: Approve.
+- No breakpoint-specific styling is required for this native-control surface.
+
+## Accessibility Requirements
+
+- Native `button` elements provide keyboard operation.
+- Every pending item exposes its actual selected state through `aria-pressed`.
+- `#approve` uses the native `disabled` attribute until a selection exists.
+- `main#review` is a polite live region so review-state changes are announced.
+- Button labels include each item's id; confirmed controls are disabled and labelled as confirmed.
+
+## Implementation Guide
+
+- `initialState(items)` normalizes items into pending, unselected entries and rejects duplicate ids.
+- `toggleSelection(state, id)` returns a new state only when `id` exists and is pending.
+- `approveSelected(state)` returns the original state when nothing is selected; otherwise it confirms selected items and clears every selection.
+- `window.reviewItems` is an optional browser seed. With no seed, the empty state is rendered.
+- Export the three pure transitions with CommonJS when it is available; the same script also mounts in a browser.
+
+## Testing Checklist
+
+- [x] State transitions cover initial, toggle, unknown-id, approval, empty approval, immutability, and duplicate-id rejection.
+- [x] Review controls use native buttons, truthful `aria-pressed`, and a disabled Approve button without a selection.
+- [ ] Rendered pixel smoke test — no browser runner is installed in this workspace; this remains for the later visual-validation phase.
+
+## Self-review
+
+**Implementation review grade**: B. The state logic and accessible control contract are fully specified and test-covered. Pixel hierarchy and responsive geometry need a browser-backed smoke test during the later audit/validation flow; no visual recipe or browser runner is available here.
